'''''Myricaria germanica''''', the '''German tamarisk''', is a species of flowering plant in the family [[Tamaricaceae]].<ref name="MYAGE" >{{cite web |url=https://gd.eppo.int/taxon/MYAGE |title=''Myricaria germanica'' (MYAGE) |author=<!--Not stated--> |date=2024 |website=EPPO Global Database |publisher=European and Mediterranean Plant Protection Organization |access-date=23 August 2024 }}</ref> It is native to continental Europe including Scandinavia, the Black Sea region, Iran, Afghanistan, and Pakistan.<ref name="POWO_827969-1" >{{cite POWO |id=827969-1 |title=''Myricaria germanica'' (L.) Desv. |access-date=23 August 2024 }}</ref> An erect shrub reaching at most {{cvt|8|ft}}, it is a [[pioneer species]] adapted to recently scoured riverbanks in mountainous regions.<ref name="IDS" >{{cite web |url=https://www.treesandshrubsonline.org/articles/myricaria/myricaria-germanica/ |title=''Myricaria germanica'' Desv. |author=<!--Not stated--> |date=2024 |website=Trees and Shrubs Online |publisher=International Dendrology Society |access-date=23 August 2024 }}</ref><ref name="catchment" >{{cite journal |title=Gene flow in a pioneer plant metapopulation (''Myricaria germanica'') at the catchment scale in a fragmented alpine river system |date=2022 |last1=Fink |first1=Sabine |last2=Hoppler-Wiedmer |first2=Andrea |last3=Zengerer |first3=Veronika |last4=Egger |first4=Gregory |last5=Schletterer |first5=Martin |last6=Scheidegger |first6=Christoph |journal=Scientific Reports |volume=12 |issue=1 |page=8570 |doi=10.1038/s41598-022-12172-x  |doi-access=free|pmid=35595737 |pmc=9122923 |bibcode=2022NatSR..12.8570F }}</ref> It has been cultivated in Great Britain since 1582.<ref name="IDS" /><ref name="RHS_45806" >{{cite web |url=https://www.rhs.org.uk/plants/45806/myricaria-germanica/details |title=''Myricaria germanica'' false tamarisk |author=<!--Not stated--> |date=2024 |website=Find a plant |publisher=The Royal Horticultural Society |access-date=23 August 2024 |quote=1 suppliers }}</ref>

==Subtaxa==
The following subspecies are accepted:<ref name=" POWO_827969-1" />
*''Myricaria germanica'' subsp. ''germanica'' – entire range, except Pakistan
*''Myricaria germanica'' subsp. ''pakistanica'' {{small|Qaiser}} – Pakistan
